{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/abyssal-exalted/1138535-sealing-the-heart-s-light-2e-abyssal-charm-peach","id":1138535,"title":"Sealing the Heart's Light (2e Abyssal Charm, PEACH)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Abyssal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-08T02:08:46-07:00","id":1138535,"title":"Sealing the Heart's Light (2e Abyssal Charm, PEACH)","content":"Hey! So in my upcoming campaign, one of the players is planning to play an Abyssal for whom Integrity and Intimacies play a central role. And while she almost certainly won't start with it, she was talking to me about a Charm she's interested in developing down the line for some potential Death Note flavored shenanigans and which I find perfectly suitable to the Abyssal theme. But I want to make sure I'm not missing anything that might be cause for pause, so I bring it to you fine Internet-folk.<br /> <br /> So, without further adieu, I give you:<br /> <br /> -------------<br /> <br /> <b><i>Sealing the Heart's Light</i></b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 4m, 1 or 3wp <b>Mins</b>: Integrity 4, Essence 3 <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Combo-Okay, Stackable<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Indefinite<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Five Hearts Hatred<br /> Many (perhaps even most) deathknights lack the internal strength necessary to purge themselves of their bonds of love, loyalty, and friendship, leaving them full of weaknesses and distractions that can be exploited to prevent them from fulfilling the Neverborns' holy mission. Those who learn this Charm are necessarily no exception, but have learned to extinguish these limiters to achieve their desired clarity - at least for a time.<br /> <br /> When activating this Charm, the Abyssal chooses one positive Intimacy they have, and fashions a metaphysical cage within their soul to entrap the Intimacy, capturing all positive associated memories (as well as the memory of using this Charm) along with it, before casting this cage Elsewhere. To the Abyssal, that positive relationship never existed. Since the memory of using the Charm is sealed away as well, retrieving these memories manually is nearly impossible, but both the memories and Intimacy will return automatically upon the fulfillment of a condition decided by the Abyssal at the time of activating the Charm (generally the completion of the mission they sealed the Intimacy to facilitate).<br /> <br /> Although very few Abyssals are willing to damage their own minds to this extent, and fewer have any reason to go to such extremes, this Charm's power can also be expanded to sealing away the character's Motivation (and positive memories associated with it, as normal) in exchange for committing three willpower instead of one. In order to do this, one must first have a second Motivation or equivalent from another source (most commonly the Abyssal using Five Hearts Hatred to generate a hatred-based Motivation in advance). The character's primary Motivation is sealed away and returns only when the character fulfills the condition set upon activation of the Charm (typically by fulfilling the replacement Motivation).<br /> <br /> Such characters are not left unscathed by hacking off such a central part of their mind like this, and find their drive and determination in this state dwindling. As normal, committed willpower can't be used while the Charm remains in effect. However, on top of this, the character's ability to regain willpower is hindered. First, the roll the Abyssal makes each morning to recover willpower receives a -2 internal penalty (this can make resting willpower recovery impossible for Abyssals with low Conviction and no supplements to this process). In addition, the character feels somewhat detached from their artificial Motivation, and loses the ability to gain willpower from making significant strides towards the success of that Motivation (though she can still gain willpower from stunts related to advancing that Motivation, as normal).<br /> <br /> The return of these memories is seldom a peaceful moment for the character, as their spirit is sent into flux by the sudden vigorous renewal of forgotten passions, either soaring high or crashing hard depending on the character's intermittent actions and experiences, as well as her goals going forward. If the character reaffirms the Intimacy and re-dedicates herself to it, she regains all her willpower points and treats the Intimacy as a Motivation for a number of days equal to her Essence+Compassion before the high wears off. However, this displeases the Neverborn greatly, and she immediately gains Resonance equal to her Essence+Whispers. (Characters with Faithful Killer's Reprieve can offset this Resonance with their restored willpower points immediately as if they were being gained from sleep, and if this would lower a Resonance rating back below 10 after it had gone above it, an involuntary Resonance burst does not occur.) A Motivation, though more draining to have sealed in the first place, can be re-implemented without issue, but also offers no willpower surge.<br /> <br /> A character who attempts to break the Intimacy or Motivation instead of letting it return, or worse yet who can't recommit to the positive relationship because it was destroyed (possibly by her own hand) while sealed, is spiritually broken, immediately losing all remaining willpower and going nearly catatonic with depression for a number of days equal to her Compassion (weeks equal to Conviction for a Motivation). For Intimacies, this crash is the worst of it, but a character who seals away her own greatest dreams and retrieves them only to find they have been stolen from her is shattered in the deepest part of her soul, additionally losing a dot of both permanent Willpower and Essence (which can be bought back later with experience).<br /> <br /> --------------<br /> <br /> So, what's the consensus? Does this seem unbalanced? Does it fail to provide the potential for intrigue, stories, and memory gambits that are hoped for, or does it succeed too well? Give me your thoughts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12682-remedy","name":"Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12682_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}